# Target C Section-125 augmented-route compression

Date: 2026-09-12

Lifecycle: audited-working proof-only reduction; theorem-state authority unchanged.
C-II and Level I remain open.

For harmonic component `r`, let `a_r` be its loaded attachment count, `L_r` its
occurrence-counted induced outer walk, `d_r=diam(P_r)`, and let `T_r,Q_r^+` be the
triangular-face count and degree-above-four defect after adding the attachment polygon
sides. Canonical Section 123 gives

```
a_r-3-s_r = (a_r-T_r+Q_r^+)/2.
```

Removing loaded-loaded contacts from the induced graph gives the exact identity
`Ltilde_r+Qtilde_r=4a_r-6-2s_r`. Adding those contacts can only shorten the outer
walk, so

```
L_r-2a_r <= a_r-T_r+Q_r^+.                         (1)
```

Summing and using the exact Section-123 dissection ledger yields

```
sum_r(L_r-2a_r) <= 2(e_BB-k-d_tile).               (2)
```

Now put

```
Delta_ad = sum_r(a_r-d_r),
A_*      = sum_r(a_r-T_r),
Q_*      = sum_r Q_r^+.
```

Since `L_r-2d_r=(L_r-2a_r)+2(a_r-d_r)`, canonical Section 122 and the cellwise
bound `P_exc,r<=5Q_r^+` imply the exact proof-only payment

```
liminf [Delta_ad + A_*/2 + 3Q_*]/D
    >= pi(2-sqrt(3))/4 = 0.210446803619233... .   (3)
```

Thus the remaining full-core obstruction is not an unconstrained exceptional-face
term. It is one of: attachment count beyond Euclidean cell diameter `Delta_ad`,
nontriangular augmented sides `A_*`, or augmented degree defect `Q_*`.

When `A_*=Q_*=o(D)`, almost every attachment side is a genuine two-edge
near-triangular tooth and (3) forces `Delta_ad >= 0.2104468D-o(D)`. The adjacent-tooth
turn inequality records a real constraint on such teeth, but its cyclic consequence
requires only a constant total base excess and therefore does not yet charge the
linear `Delta_ad` term. No exact unit triangle or strict diameter descent follows.

All statements retain occurrence multiplicity and contact-isolated source points;
the Section-57 affine kernel is used only on the nonisolated core. The reduction is
finite before the final Section-122 limit and makes no local/global face-injectivity
claim beyond the canonical Section-123 bound.
